{
 "version": 1,
 "doc": [
  "Discovery facts per layout repo of go_layouts (spec §3, master plan C4/C10), written by hand from the go",
  "command's rules; never generated from discovery output. Each top-level directory is its own repo (repo name =",
  "directory name); _outside/ is not a repo. Paths are relative to the layout repo root. Per repo:",
  "units: module path -> {root, go, toolchain, vendor (the module's own consistent vendor/), group, requires",
  "[path, version, indirect], replaces (local `new` relative to the repo root; outside the repo it starts with",
  "../), in_repo_deps (unit keys whose in-repo source the unit compiles: imported packages of modules reached",
  "through the group's go.work use or a local replace)}. groups: '<kind>:<go.work dir or module root, . = repo",
  "root>' -> {kind, modules, vendor, degraded, status, pattern, warnings_contain (substrings of the group's",
  "warnings)}. files: relpath -> owning unit (null = no module, absent from unit_of_file). scanned_files: the",
  "number of files scan_go_files returns; not_scanned: relpaths it must not return; skipped: skip counts by",
  "reason, counted in .go files, except that a symlinked directory is not entered and counts once",
  "('symlink-dir') and dot directories are not entered nor counted. warnings_contain: substrings of the repo's",
  "warnings (group warnings included). modes: evaluate's offline mode (empty module cache, GOPROXY=off) and env",
  "mode (download mode against file:///.../test_codes/_proxy): module_source, missing_modules per group",
  "('path@version'; only groups with status ok and no vendor report them), and status_after_load where the",
  "load changes a group's status (amendment R5)."
 ],
